    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d286-a4">

                <pb facs="0464" n="368" xml:id="pg368"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 383.—Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Day.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-05-09"><hi rendition="#italic">May 9,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I received the following from the foreign office this morning: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Extract from telegram from Governor Sir F. Cardew to Mr. Chamberlain:
                            “Regret to inform you that following American missionaries, Mr. and Mrs.
                            Cain, Misses Archer, Hatfield, and Schenck, killed by insurgent bands at
                            Rotifunk; but Miss Ward, as well as following American missionaries, Mr.
                            and Mrs. Burtner and Mr. and Mrs. Minshall, from Shengeh, and Miss
                            Mullen, from Mamaligi, are here quite safe.” Please inform American
                            ambassador.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hay.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
